+## Notes
+
+<a name="notes"></a>
+
+- **Node 25.** Node 25 ships a built-in `localStorage` global that has no Web Storage methods unless a
+  backing file is configured. Wallet libraries feature-detect the global and then crash on
+  `localStorage.getItem()` during server render and static export. `packages/nextjs/scripts/run-next.mjs`
+  wraps every Next command and adds `--no-experimental-webstorage` to `NODE_OPTIONS` — at the process
+  level, so Next's build workers inherit it — but only when that global is actually present, so older
+  Node versions (which reject the unknown flag) are unaffected. Nothing to configure.
+- **Why the frontend targets `chains.foundry` and not `chains.base`.** The fork keeps chain id 31337.
+  `scaffold.config.ts` holds a single literal chain on purpose: the contract hooks derive their types
+  from it, so a union of chains would erase `TipJar` from the known contract names. DEPLOY.md covers
+  the switch to Base.
+- **USDC has 6 decimals**, not 18. Amounts in the contract and in `cast` calls are base units:
+  1 USDC = `1000000`.
+- **The jar's owner can always withdraw.** `renounceOwnership()` is overridden to revert: `withdraw`
+  is the only way tips leave the contract, so renouncing would strand every tip received afterwards.
+
+## Useful commands
+
+| Command | What it does |
+| --- | --- |
+| `yarn fork --network base` | Anvil forking Base, chain id 31337, 1s blocks |
+| `yarn deploy` | Deploy `TipJar` to the fork and regenerate the frontend ABIs |
+| `yarn fund [addresses...]` | Move real USDC from a whale to demo identities on the fork |
+| `yarn start` | Next.js dev server on http://localhost:3000 |
+| `yarn test` | Foundry unit + fork tests |
+| `yarn lint` / `yarn format` | Lint / format both packages |
+| `yarn chain` | Plain Anvil, no Base state — the tip jar cannot be deployed against it |
+
